  "body": "The maintainer reported this in chat on 2026-11-15, on the v0.21.0 tree.\n\nHis words: \"The Orbit control has changed - It is not rotating around where the mouse pointer is clicking anymore... is that intentional? which issue introduced that?\"\n\nWhat happens: an orbit drag turns the view about the camera target (`Camera::target`, `crates/ui/src/viewport.rs`). The point under the pointer moves on the screen during the drag.\n\nExpected: the orbit turns about the model point under the pointer at the press. That point stays at its screen position during the drag. If the press is on empty space, the orbit turns about the camera target.\n\nFirst reading of the history (the orchestrator session, read-only):\n\n- `Camera::orbit` changes only `yaw` and `pitch`. The two call sites are in `crates/ui/src/egui_app/shell.rs`. No commit in the history of these files moves the pivot to the picked point.\n- Thus no commit that removed a pointer pivot was found. The cause can be a change of the camera target, not of the orbit.\n- Candidates for a changed target or drag: `41c54108b` (camera tools in the control ribbon, 2026-11-14), the framing code (`State` \"Center the orbit camera on the document's bounding sphere\"), `c0b4dfc85` (work envelope display, 2026-11-15).\n\nFor the work:\n\n- Compare the orbit on the v0.20.0 build and the v0.21.0 build with the same project. Record where the camera target is after open, after a frame and after a wheel zoom.\n- If a commit changed the target, name it here and restore the behaviour.\n- If no commit changed it, add the pointer pivot: take the pick point at the press, turn about it, and keep `Camera::target` consistent for pan, zoom and `frame`. The same rule applies in perspective and orthographic projection.\n- Record the choice in `docs/decisions/`.\n\nDone means:\n\n- A test pins that the picked point keeps its screen position during an orbit drag, in each projection.\n- A test pins the fallback for a press on empty space.\n- A comment here names the commit that changed the behaviour, or says that no commit changed it.\n",
